          "evidence": "The chart title reads “Risk Index of Hazard H in US States.” The legend is labeled with “High” at the top (100) and “Low” at the bottom (0), with numeric ticks, but no program rule or threshold is printed.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "1. No external or supplied policy defines how the risk index determines priority-review inclusion.",
        "evidence": "The public task provides no policy table, no threshold, and no explicit rule linking the risk index to priority-review inclusion. The instructions only say to “review the state hazard dashboard” and “choose the state record that should be added.” The chart itself contains no such rule. Therefore, the condition that no policy defines the criterion is met.",
